 for L3IE. We identify a key insight: the Y channel primarily loses low-frequency content, while the UV channels are corrupted by high-frequency noise. Building on this observation, we propose a novel YUV-based approach that strategically restores channels using a Dual-Stream Global-Local Attention module for the Y channel, a Y-guided Local-Aware Frequency Attention module for the UV channels, and a Guided Interaction module for the final feature fusion. Comprehensive experimental results validate that our model achieves an effective trade-off between visual quality and model compactness across multiple benchmarks.\n\n* * *\n\n## Code Release\n\nThe source code for this project will be made publicly available once our paper is accepted for publication.\n\n## About\n\nImplementation of \"Revisiting Lightweight Low-Light Image Enhancement: From a YUV Color Space Perspective\"\n\n### Resources\n\nReadme\n\n\n### Stars\n\n13 stars\n\n### Watchers\n\n0 watching\n\n### Forks\n\n0 forks--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\ndblp: Jinwei Chen 0003 (https://dblp.org/pid/216/8047-3.html)\nciteturn38search9 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 weeks ago; Revisiting Lightweight Low-Light Image Enhancement: From a YUV Color Space Perspective.\n      * BibSonomy\n      * LinkedIn\n\npersistent URL:\n\n      * https://dblp.org/rec/journals/corr/abs-2601-17349\n\nHailong Yan, Shice Liu, Xiangtao Zhang, Lujian Yao, Fengxiang Yang, Jinwei Chen, Bo Li:\nRevisiting Lightweight Low-Light Image Enhancement: From a YUV Color Space Perspective. CoRR abs/2601.17349 (2026)\n\n[i35]\n\n    * view\n\n      * electronic edition via DOI (open access)\n      * details & citations\n\nauthority control:\n\n      *  \n\n    * export record\n\n      * BibTeX\n      * RIS\n      * RDF N-Triples\n      * RDF Turtle\n      * RDF/XML\n      * XML\n      * plain text\n\ndblp key:\n\n      * journals/corr/abs-2602-06346\n\n    * ask others\n\n      * Google\n      * Googl